 "notes": "Hydrology report on the unsaturated zone; geology is brief (page 10). Monitoring sites recorded as 'other' observations with ground elevations from Table 1 (page 14). Instrument positions, tensions, saturations, tracer rates and conductance curves (pages 14-34) are not recorded; the compacted clayey-sand cap/barrier is engineered fill and its properties are skipped. Figure pages 15-19, 21-23, 25-34 are graphs with garbled text. Ksat table on page 21 has a garbled text layer; units header reads 'Ksat(C/n/S)' (cm/s). Packet 2 continues the report.\nContinues packet 1. Tritium concentrations (Table 3, page 37), tracer velocities, model grid details and error analysis are not recorded (not geologic units or aquifer properties). Graph pages 36, 38, 40, 42-44 have garbled labels. References: kept South Carolina site and regional entries; skipped general methods and national references (ASTM, Bowen, Brooks and Corey, Brutsaert, Campbell, Davis and Neuman, Drever, EPA, Freeze and Cherry, Freeze and Witherspoon, Hung, Neff, Purcell, state health department 1984 monitoring report, Thatcher and others, NOAA, Winter).",
